<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Library</OutputType>
    <Platforms>AnyCPU</Platforms>
    <Product>SRT Demo Payload Contracts</Product>
    <Description>Payload types published by the demo producer.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    A payload-contract assembly, and the pattern every real producer should follow.

    It holds the DTOs and nothing else: no dependency on the producer, no dependency on
    SRTPluginBase, no logic. The producer and every consumer reference THIS, which is what lets a
    consumer decode a producer's data without referencing the producer assembly.

    That reference was the concrete failing of the previous generation: the RE4 overlay was declared
    as PluginBase<SRTPluginProducerRE4R>, a hard binary dependency on the producer class. It could
    not survive a process boundary, and it should not have survived in-process either.
  -->

</Project>
